>>
Rule 1 (input must be 3D or higher to avoid "Expected 3D or higher dimensionality")
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3
>>
Rule 2 (disallow complex dtypes to avoid "avg_pool2d not implemented for 'ComplexDouble'")
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 3 (disallow uint8 to avoid "avg_pool3d_out_frame not implemented for 'Byte'")
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 5
>>
Rule 4 (size must be positive, odd, and not exceed channels to avoid negative kernel/pad and narrow length issues)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= v_2 ≥ 1 ∧ v_2 % 2 = 1 ∧ v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 5 (channels dimension must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 6 (bound tensor dimensionality and each dimension size to avoid OOM and storage overflow)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≤ 6 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, i) ≤ 1000000
>>
Rule 7 (stability of normalization: non-negative alpha and strictly positive beta, k)
{v_3 : float, v_4 : float, v_5 : float} |= v_3 ≥ 0 ∧ v_4 > 0 ∧ v_5 > 0
>>
Rule 8 (ensure effective kernel and padding are valid by requiring non-negative, bounded window size)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 ≥ 1 then v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, 1) else false
